Article 1. Definitions

1.1 "Licensor" means ShinoyukiMiyako (the natural person in whom the rights vest)
    and World of Kivotos (the operating entity), jointly or severally.

1.2 "the Software" means the entire contents of this repository (Wok-Project),
    including without limitation source code, build scripts, configuration files,
    datapacks, art assets such as models and textures, audio assets, design
    documents, code comments, commit history, and everything compiled, generated
    or derived therefrom.

1.3 "Official Build" means the miningdim mod jar officially released by the
    Licensor, and any other distribution form expressly designated as official
    by the Licensor.

1.4 "Official Server" means a Minecraft server operated by the Licensor, or
    operated under the Licensor's written authorization.

1.5 "End User" means a natural person player who installs and runs an Official
    Build for the purpose of playing on an Official Server.

1.6 "Authorized Collaborator" means a natural person expressly granted write
    access or contributor status to this repository by the Licensor in writing.

1.7 "Written Authorization" means a document signed by the Licensor, or an
    electronic authorization expressly issued from the Licensor's official
    accounts (including the GitHub organization account and official announcement
    channels). Oral permission, community chatter, and unanswered requests do not
    constitute Written Authorization.

Article 2. Reservation of Rights

2.1 The Software is proprietary software. It is not open source, not free
    software, and not in the public domain. The Licensor retains all copyright
    and all other intellectual property rights in the Software.

2.2 All rights not expressly granted in Articles 4 and 5 are reserved by the
    Licensor. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, no implied
    license, license by estoppel, exhaustion of rights, or similar doctrine
    shall apply.

2.3 The accessibility of the Software on GitHub or any code hosting platform --
    including that the source may be viewed, that the platform offers
    fork/clone/download controls, or that it is indexed by search engines or
    code indexing services -- does not constitute any grant of license, nor any
    acquiescence by the Licensor to the acts listed in Article 3. The existence
    of such platform features does not diminish the binding effect of this
    Agreement.

2.4 The minimal, transitory copying automatically performed by the platform's
    own technology solely in the course of ordinary in-browser viewing of the
    Software shall not be deemed a breach. This exception is strictly limited to
    the act of viewing and does not extend to local retention, cloning,
    mirroring, or any other reproduction.

Article 3. Prohibited Acts

Except as expressly permitted by Articles 4 and 5, no person may perform, assist
another in performing, or facilitate another's performance of, any of the
following, including without limitation:

  (1) copying, downloading, cloning, forking, mirroring, archiving, or otherwise
      reproducing all or any part of the Software;
  (2) modifying, translating, adapting, refactoring, or creating derivative
      works based on the Software;
  (3) distributing, publishing, publicly transmitting, publicly displaying,
      lending, renting, selling, reselling, sublicensing, or otherwise making
      all or any part of the Software available to any third party;
  (4) uploading to or listing on CurseForge, Modrinth, MCBBS, or any other
      third-party mod distribution platform, modpack, resource site, cloud
      drive, mirror, or public code hosting repository;
  (5) decompiling, disassembling, or reverse engineering an Official Build, or
      by any means extracting, recovering, or deducing the Software's source
      code, algorithms, numeric tables, balance parameters, economic model, or
      data structures;
  (6) reimplementing, cloning the functionality of, or porting the Software --
      including porting to other Minecraft versions, other mod loaders, or other
      games -- by reference to its implementation, numeric design, system
      architecture, or interaction design;
  (7) using any part of the Software (including source code, comments,
      documentation, art assets, and Official Builds) to train, fine-tune,
      distill, or evaluate any machine learning model or artificial intelligence
      system, or including it in any retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) corpus,
      vector index, code search index, or public dataset;
  (8) using the Software for any commercial purpose, including without
      limitation paid servers, paid modpacks, paid server management, subscription
      hosting services, and any for-profit activity in which the Software is a
      selling point or component;
  (9) removing, obscuring, altering, or rendering imperceptible any copyright
      notice, license notice, authorship attribution, version identifier, or
      watermark in the Software;
 (10) circumventing, cracking, or assisting in circumventing any license check,
      server binding, anti-cheat mechanism, or other technical protection
      measure in the Software.

Article 4. Limited End User License (Official Builds Only)

4.1 The Licensor hereby grants End Users a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
    non-sublicensable, revocable-at-will, worldwide limited license to:
      (a) install an Official Build into the mods directory of a Minecraft
          client they personally own;
      (b) run the Official Build for the purpose of ordinary gameplay while
          connected to an Official Server;
      (c) make the technical copies necessarily incidental to (a) and (b),
          including automatic client-side download, loading into memory,
          on-disk caching, and runtime extraction.

4.2 Scope limits: this Article grants no right to modify, redistribute, operate
    independently of an Official Server, extract art or data assets, repackage
    into a modpack, or run an Official Build on any unofficial server. The
    prohibitions in Article 3 continue to apply to End Users throughout the term
    of this license.

4.3 This license terminates automatically when the End User's eligibility to play
    on an Official Server ends (including by ban, departure, or server shutdown).
    The Licensor may also revoke this license, in whole or as to any individual,
    at any time by public notice, without stating a reason and without incurring
    any obligation to compensate. Upon termination, the End User shall
    immediately delete all copies in their possession.

Article 5. Authorized Collaborator Exception and Contribution Assignment

5.1 An Authorized Collaborator may, to the extent necessary to contribute to this
    project, clone this repository, build and run it locally, modify the code,
    and submit Pull Requests to this repository.

5.2 The foregoing license is strictly limited to the purpose of contributing to
    this repository and may not be used for any other purpose. It terminates
    automatically when the collaborator's contributor status ends. Upon
    termination, the collaborator shall delete all local copies, build outputs,
    and derivatives in their possession and shall neither retain nor repurpose
    them.

5.3 Contribution assignment: any contribution submitted to this repository, once
    merged or otherwise accepted in any form, shall be deemed to grant the
    Licensor a worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, sublicensable, exclusive, and
    royalty-free license to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, sublicense, and
    commercialize that contribution in any manner. To the extent permitted by
    applicable law, the contributor waives all moral rights in the contribution
    other than the right of attribution. The contributor warrants that the
    contribution is their own original work, infringes no third party's
    intellectual property rights, and is not subject to any third-party license
    conflicting with this Agreement (including without limitation copyleft
    licenses of the GPL family).

Article 6. Third-Party Components

6.1 This Agreement applies only to content owned by the Licensor. Third-party
