Article 10. Breach, Termination, and Remedies

10.1 Any breach of this Agreement automatically terminates all licenses granted
     to the breaching party hereunder, effective as of the moment of breach and
     without notice from the Licensor.

10.2 Upon termination, the breaching party shall immediately cease all use and
     destroy all copies, derivatives, and build outputs of the Software in their
     possession or control.

10.3 The breaching party shall bear all losses caused to the Licensor by the
     breach, including the reasonable costs incurred by the Licensor in stopping
     the infringement, gathering evidence, and enforcing its rights (including
     attorneys' fees, notarization fees, and litigation costs).

10.4 Because the Software's source code, numeric design, and economic model
     cannot be restored by monetary compensation once disclosed, the Licensor is
     entitled to seek injunctive relief and other interim or permanent remedies
     in respect of a breach, without the need to separately prove that the harm
     is irreparable.

10.5 The Licensor reserves all rights to pursue civil, administrative, and
     criminal liability for infringement. No failure or delay by the Licensor in
     exercising any right hereunder shall operate as a waiver of that right, and
     no single or partial exercise shall preclude any further exercise of that
